  "section_notes": "The final text keeps the 5% per-model ceiling and 55°C test, but removes any sales stop: a model above 5% can keep selling indefinitely unless the regulator finds an imminent or unmitigated risk, which mainly protects Northwind's Hearth 10 at 6.2%. Mandatory recall is set at 8 per 100k with no transition, so Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9 would be captured if its rate is validated. Remote shut-off retrofit runs six years (favouring Northwind) and suppression starts at 36 months (within the acceptable range)."
